        "original_id": "79f26c35-9ffb-5e04-b72c-3f5e0c06c488",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ivor Gurney, Robert Walser, Iain Burnside\n- Works: A Soldier and a Maker, Ein Tagebuch, Jakob von Gunten\n- Roles: poet, composer, writer\n\nFacts:\n- Robert Walser was a German-speaking Swiss writer who lived from 15 April 1878 to 25 December 1956.\n- Ivor Gurney was an English poet and composer, particularly of songs, who lived from 28 August 1890 to 26 December 1937.\n- Ein Tagebuch is a novel by Swiss writer Robert Walser that was first published in German in 1909.\n- A Soldier and a Maker is a piece of musical theatre by Iain Burnside about the life story of the First World War poet and composer Ivor Gurney.\n- Jakob von Gunten is associated with the novel titled Ein Tagebuch.",
